"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[61028],{461028:e=>{e.exports="# Temporary Tables & CTEs\n\nRedshift temp table patterns → DBSQL TEMP TABLEs, temporary views, CTEs, and staging tables.\n\n## REDSHIFT\n\n### Temporary tables\n\nRedshift `CREATE TEMP TABLE` / `CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE` creates a session-scoped table; it also supports PostgreSQL-style leading-hash-free names (no `#temp` prefix).\n\n**Critical limitations of DBSQL TEMP TABLE:**\n\n1. **SQL warehouse sessions only** — Not supported in notebook or job contexts running on classic or serverless compute clusters; only available inside a SQL warehouse session.\n2. **No `ALTER TABLE`** — Cannot add/drop columns after creation.\n3. **Session-scoped** — Dropped automatically when the session ends.\n\n```sql\n-- Redshift\nCREATE TEMP TABLE staging AS SELECT * FROM source WHERE active = 1;\n\n-- DBSQL (SQL warehouse session)\nCREATE TEMP TABLE staging AS SELECT * FROM my_catalog.my_schema.source WHERE active = 1;\n```\n\n**Preferred alternatives** (for notebook / classic compute context):\n\n```sql\n-- CTEs (best for single-query scope)\nWITH staging AS (SELECT * FROM source WHERE active = 1)\nSELECT * FROM staging;\n\n-- Temporary views (session-scoped, work on serverless compute)\nCREATE OR REPLACE TEMPORARY VIEW staging AS\nSELECT * FROM source WHERE active = 1;\n\n-- Permanent staging tables in Unity Catalog (most flexible for multi-step ETL)\nCREATE TABLE my_catalog.staging.tmp AS SELECT ...;\n-- ... use ...\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS my_catalog.staging.tmp;\n```\n\nStrip Redshift layout hints (`DISTSTYLE`, `DISTKEY`, `SORTKEY`, `ENCODE`) — see `01-schema-and-storage.md`.\n\n### `CREATE TEMP TABLE ... AS SELECT` (CTAS)\n\nIdentical syntax; strip Redshift layout hints:\n\n```sql\n-- Redshift\nCREATE TEMP TABLE customer_totals DISTSTYLE EVEN AS\nSELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id;\n\n-- DBSQL\nCREATE TEMP TABLE customer_totals AS\nSELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id;\n```\n\n### Cross-session / global temp tables\n\nRedshift has **no global temp tables**. All `TEMP TABLE` objects are session-scoped. If a Redshift workload needs cross-session visibility, it uses a permanent staging table or schema. Translate 1:1 — permanent staging table under Unity Catalog with a DROP afterwards:\n\n```sql\n-- Redshift (permanent staging schema, manually dropped)\nCREATE TABLE staging.tmp_orders AS SELECT * FROM source;\n-- ... use across multiple sessions/tasks ...\nDROP TABLE staging.tmp_orders;\n\n-- DBSQL (three-part name + unique suffix to avoid concurrent-run collisions)\nCREATE TABLE my_catalog.staging.tmp_orders_run_12345 AS SELECT * FROM my_catalog.source.orders;\n-- ... use ...\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS my_catalog.staging.tmp_orders_run_12345;\n```\n\n**Naming strategy under concurrent pipeline runs**: include a run identifier (`{{ job.run_id }}` in a Databricks Workflow) or a UUID generated before the pipeline starts to avoid parallel executions clobbering each other.\n\n### CTEs\n\nRedshift and DBSQL CTE syntax is identical:\n\n```sql\n-- Redshift / DBSQL\nWITH active_customers AS (\n    SELECT customer_id FROM customers WHERE status = 'active'\n),\nrecent_orders AS (\n    SELECT * FROM orders WHERE order_date >= CURRENT_DATE - INTERVAL '30 days'\n)\nSELECT c.customer_id, o.order_id\nFROM active_customers c\nJOIN recent_orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id;\n```\n\n### ON COMMIT — drop the clause\n\n`ON COMMIT {PRESERVE ROWS | DELETE ROWS | DROP}` is PostgreSQL-standard but **not a Redshift feature** — Redshift silently accepts or rejects it depending on the source, and temp tables always persist until session end. If the source was ported from PostgreSQL and still carries the clause, drop it: DBSQL temp tables have no commit-time lifecycle either.\n\n### Table expressions in procedures\n\nRedshift PL/pgSQL supports `CREATE TEMP TABLE` inside a procedure body. DBSQL supports this pattern only in SQL warehouse context (where temp tables are available). For notebook/classic compute, rewrite as CTE or temporary view inside the procedure.\n"}}]);
